+## R-TRANSFER: code as data, then exact candidate
+
+The only path is CIP-0009 D5a's eight-step round: **materialize, work, round end, export, candidate, review, rework, integration**. The caller supplies admitted repository commit B's bounded canonical tree archive; the dispatcher relays/journals it and holds no repository. `swarma-workspace-materialize` writes a fresh standalone private repository under the child UID, no remotes/hooks/credential helpers. The plan digest binds B, path-to-blob-id manifest digest, task write scope and exec profile. Validators stay outside write scope unless the task is about them; dependencies are platform-seeded read-only caches. Worker Git history is never imported. The worker has no network, push or merge-request access.
+
+A remote signed final envelope (local board outcome) ends the round. Account-wide confirmed absence and a workplace write fence precede `swarma-workspace-export` under the child UID with fixed environment/no network. It walks without following links, skips Git administration and emits only changed regular-file content/executable bit, symlink text and deletions against the manifest. File-count/per-file/total/binary caps are unpublished. RWP v2.1 §8/§10 gates are adopted: special files, `.git` path components however spelled, case-fold/Unicode-normalisation collisions, gitlinks/submodules, root escapes and exceeded caps refuse the whole export. No partial output. Dispatcher journals digests and returns the result only to the original run requester; the board accepts it as a resource. Export cleanup obligation blocks home deletion until recorded export or an explicit operator waiver. An intermediate turn-boundary export uses the same fence/absence requirements.
+
+The orchestrator's deterministic board import builds on B in a scratch index, hooks disabled and no attribute filters/drivers. Hard refusals are `.git` components, outside-write-scope paths and `.task-board/` changes. Flagged paths are CI (`.github/**`, `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `.circleci/**`), Git behaviour (`.gitattributes`, `.gitmodules`), hooks/auto-run (`.githooks/**`, `.husky/**`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, `lefthook.yml`, `.envrc`, `.vscode/**`), agent instructions/configuration (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` anywhere, `.claude/**`, `.codex/**`, `.agents/**`, `.mcp.json`) and all symlinks. C is signed by repository identity, with worker/run/result-digest trailers; its tree equals independent recomputation from B plus change set.
+
+A trusted reviewer, neither untrusted-class nor producer identity, reviews exactly C. K1 acceptance never transfers by patch equality; every flagged hunk needs explicit verdict acknowledgement. All candidate execution uses R-VERIFY; untrusted candidates are never pushed before acceptance where CI would run with secrets. Changes requested record findings and send a signed task letter with C as the next admitted base; the donor session continues, the workplace is freshly materialized, old workspace removed only after recorded export, and C2 builds on C. Local rework is a new run with findings. Questions use ordinary letters/outcomes. Accepted exact head integrates only by board signed fast-forward K1/K3; moved base requires ordinary refresh/re-review. RWP exporter ownership differs only in using an approved child-UID executor rather than the harness/container-volume reader.
+
+## R-NET-TOOL, R-EXEC and R-VERIFY
+
+Workplaces have zero egress and denied loopback, no proxy destination: Linux qualified per-execution namespace without external interfaces plus Unix-socket-only address families; macOS qualified network-denying sandbox and per-UID deny. Platform hosts bind neither `direct` nor `external-http-proxy` to any account; operator machines without the platform retain those/cooperative profiles. Local trusted agents use provider endpoints through bound profile proxies; one listener per generation, own port, allowlists/no mail ports, private/metadata dial guard, attributable caps/logs belong to N15, not this wire protocol. Runner dependency egress follows the same proxy requirements.
+
+Default donor loop reaches only model-provider endpoints and our host; no search/fetch tool or donor-side web server, no internet in the project environment. CIP-0008 lockdown plan alone disables provider-side search inside the provider API, invisible to network rules. Outside web content mixes contexts and invites injection. Tasks instead carry trusted-side checked resources as board resources and signed-task-letter attachments, read-only next to the workspace with plan digests; data, never instructions. More resources are requested by letter/outcome; the worker never fetches.
+
+An operator act at admission may admit a remote worker to the trusted circle for per-identity donor-side web opt-in only, never the untrusted class. Options remain pending qualification: provider-side search under a new CIP-0008 tuple proving provider execution/no local fetch, or platform-shipped donor MCP `swarma-web`. The latter uses its own B identity or C sandbox, never harness/bridge identity; egress is search-provider API endpoints only, never arbitrary fetch. It holds the donor's own key there (A: donor Keychain or 0600 file), donor consent at `init`; no key crosses channel/frames/packages, and no project method requests it. Results reach only the donor model. The harness keeps provider-only egress; other lockdown controls stay.
+
+R-EXEC is an OS executable allowlist per task class, with non-executable writable areas. Excluded for all agent classes: compilers/linkers/transpilers/bundlers, test runners, package managers/installers, containers/VMs, network tools and harness/agent binaries. Editing, local Git inspection/search and qualified light type checks are admitted by profile. Shared light/heavy executables need a D-PATH protected fixed-subcommand wrapper proving heavy forms refuse; interpreters only as needed, bounded by ceilings. No account starts its own loop/environment. All heavy work and all worker-code execution use R-VERIFY secret-free isolated ephemeral runners on another machine with controlled dependency egress; downloads only there. Tester orchestrates and reads board data in testing state, never executes candidate code. `agent-headless-build` is withdrawn for agent accounts.
+
+## R-UNTRUSTED, R-STANDING and abuse-control admission
+
+Record the class at registration/admission, never from names. Every workplace is untrusted unless admitted to the trusted circle by an operator act; zero egress, exec profile, transfer/review and all host boundaries remain. Broker refuses subscription bindings/leases; no workplace receives one. Slice 0/user-manager v0 refuse the untrusted class (code unpublished). A long-lived standing workplace is allowed, loop at donor only; standing loops on our host are trusted-class only. Trusted standing harness settings/hooks/MCP/instructions come from plan, digest-checked before launch/restart/native resume or root-owned outside home; drift refuses and repair is explicit re-materialization.
+
+R-CEILINGS admits by qualified per-OS-release hard/soft/absent capability matrix, never OS-name exclusion. Untrusted requires hard process ceiling, enforced egress, exec profile, isolated temporary areas and hard memory/CPU/disk where available; acceptability of soft substitutes is an open owner decision recorded per host by operator act. CIP-0009 D5d states the selected Linux non-delegated R-FATE unit, kernel baseline and macOS reference/gaps. R-RANGE-DENY preinstalls default deny for UIDs 30000–59999; v0 proxy-only becomes v1 bound-profile/zero narrowing. Dedicated-test-UID precedence probes run at install, service starts and verification schedule across anchors/interfaces/loopback/tunnels; failure drops enforced readiness. R-SOCKETS checks reachable sockets equal the declared platform set. R-SHARED refuses untrusted placements beside shared services; platform services are exempt, public join ingress lives separately.
+
+R-WATCH samples per-UID CPU/memory/process/home-disk/network/refused-connection counters including mail ports, with least-privileged read-only sampler and per-class thresholds. Hard threshold requests one-account egress freeze and journaled dispatcher `exec.stop`, never unjournaled kill; phone-path alerts, node stop manual. R-ALLSTOP is a narrowing operator act refused inside agent sessions, phone authentication/one confirmation or terminal fallback: dispatcher hold, range deny-all, account-wide journaled stop/confirmed absence for every generation, broker lease/renewal freeze (delivered tokens retain vendor lifetime), session-host delivery closure/board snapshots. Each service journals; partial/unknown keeps admission closed; recovery explicit, no automatic restart. Workplace suspended and donor channel-down behaviour handle both paths, with no new state. Thresholds/interfaces/act/record formats remain unpublished.
